export const terms = "**Effective date:** October 15, 2026 · **Version:** 1.0\n\n## 1. Who we are and what these terms cover\n\nRenoSwap (\"RenoSwap,\" \"we,\" \"us\") is run by RenoSwap LLC. RenoSwap LLC is a Texas limited liability company. RenoSwap is a website that helps people swap, sell, or give away leftover renovation and construction materials.\n\nThese Terms of Service (\"Terms\") are a contract between you and us. They cover your use of renoswap.com, renoswap.vercel.app, and any other RenoSwap site or app (together, the \"Service\"). By creating an account or using the Service, you agree to these Terms, our [Privacy Policy](/privacy), and our [Prohibited Items list](/prohibited). If you don't agree, please don't use RenoSwap.\n\n## 2. Who can use RenoSwap\n\n- You must be **18 or older**.\n- You must give us accurate information and keep it up to date.\n- One person per account. Keep your password private. You're responsible for what happens under your account.\n- If you use RenoSwap for a business (for example, as a contractor), you confirm you're allowed to act for that business, and these Terms apply to the business too.\n- RenoSwap is based in Texas and is open across the United States. Listings need a valid U.S. ZIP code.\n\n## 3. What RenoSwap does, and doesn't do\n\nRenoSwap is **only a venue**: a place for users to connect. We are **not** a party to any swap, sale, or giveaway between users, we are not a buyer, seller, broker, or agent, and we are **not responsible or liable for meetups, pickups, or deliveries** between users.\n\n- **We don't handle payment for materials.** Buyers and sellers arrange payment (cash, Venmo, Zelle, etc.) and pickup or shipping themselves. RenoSwap never holds money for materials and takes no cut of sales.\n- **We don't inspect, test, store, or deliver items, and we don't guarantee them.** We don't guarantee that any item is as described, safe, legal, up to code, or fit for your project.\n- **We don't check users' backgrounds.** A \"Contractor\" label means the user says they are a contractor or is on the Contractor plan. It is **not** a license check or endorsement.\n- **Admin review is limited.** An admin looks at listings before they go public. That review is a quick check against our rules, not an inspection or a promise that the listing is accurate or lawful.\n\nYou deal with other users at your own risk. Use good judgment and read our [safety tips](/safety).\n\n## 4. Listings\n\n**Listing types.** You can list items as:\n\n- **Swap:** trade for other materials.\n- **Sell:** for a price you set.\n- **Sell or Swap:** either one.\n- **Fast & Free:** a free giveaway with a pickup timer. The timer starts when an admin approves the listing, and the listing expires when the timer runs out.\n\n**Your promises when you list.** You promise that:\n\n- You own the item or have the right to give or sell it. For example, leftover materials from a client's job belong to whoever paid for them unless they told you otherwise.\n- Your description and photos are honest and are photos of the actual item. You disclose known defects, damage, age, and anything a reasonable person would want to know, especially possible **lead paint** (painted items from before 1978) or **asbestos**.\n- The item isn't on our [Prohibited Items list](/prohibited) and isn't illegal to sell or give away.\n- Listings are for **physical materials, fixtures, and tools**, not services (like labor or installs), job ads, or ads for other businesses.\n\n**Our rights.** We can refuse, edit the display of, pause, expire, or remove any listing at any time, for any reason or no reason, including after it was approved. Non-free listings may expire after about 45 days.\n\n**Distance.** Browse shows an **approximate** distance (for example, \"~12 mi\") calculated from ZIP codes, not exact addresses. It's an estimate only; confirm the pickup location with the other user.\n\n**Photos.** When you upload a photo, the app removes GPS location data stored in the image file. Still, don't photograph anything that shows your address.\n\n**Deals.** An offer or message on RenoSwap is not a binding contract with us. Any deal is only between you and the other user.\n\n## 5. Messages, offers, and reports\n\n- Use messages and offers only to talk about listings. No spam, harassment, threats, hate, or scams.\n- Don't ask for or share sensitive information like bank logins, Social Security numbers, or ID photos.\n- You can **report** a listing or user. Reports go to our admins, who decide what to do.\n- To keep people safe and enforce these Terms, our admins **can read messages, offers, and reports** when needed (for example, when something is reported). See the [Privacy Policy](/privacy).\n\n**Ratings and reviews.** After both users confirm a trade, each can leave a 1–5 star rating and an optional comment. Reviews must be honest and about that trade. Don't fake trades to boost ratings. We may hide or remove reviews that break these Terms.\n\n**Email alerts.** We email you about new offers and messages and, if you set them up, \"Looking for\" alerts when matching listings are approved. You can turn these off on the Account page or with the unsubscribe link in any alert email. We'll still send required account emails (like sign-up confirmations and password resets).\n\n## 6. Plans, payments, and refunds\n\n**Free plan.** Up to **3 active listings** (active means pending review, approved, or claimed).\n\n**Paid plans (monthly subscriptions):**\n\n| Plan | Price | Active listings |\n|---|---|---|\n| Homeowner | $4.99/month | up to 10 |\n| Contractor | $19/month | up to 25, plus a Contractor badge |\n\n**Listing boost:** **$1.99 one-time** per listing. A boosted listing is shown near the top of Browse for **7 days**.\n\n- **Payments are processed by Stripe.** We never see or store your full card number. Stripe's own terms and privacy policy also apply.\n- **Subscriptions renew automatically every month** until you cancel. By subscribing, you authorize us (through Stripe) to charge your payment method each month.\n- **Switching plans.** If you switch between Homeowner and Contractor, Stripe adjusts the charge for the rest of the month (a prorated credit or charge).\n- **Canceling.** Cancel anytime from **Billing → Manage billing**. Your plan stays active until the end of the period you already paid for, then returns to Free. If you then have more active listings than the Free plan allows, your existing listings aren't deleted, but you can't post new ones until you're under the limit.\n- **Refunds.** Payments are **non-refundable**, including partial months, **unless the law requires a refund**. Boosts are **non-refundable once applied**. If we remove your boosted listing for breaking our rules, you don't get a refund. If we make a billing mistake, contact us and we'll fix it.\n- **Price changes.** We may change prices. We'll tell you at least 30 days before a new price applies to your subscription, and you can cancel before then.\n- **Taxes.** Prices may not include applicable sales tax. If tax applies, it will be shown at checkout.\n- **Failed payments.** If a payment fails, your paid plan may end and your account goes back to Free.\n\n## 7. Your content\n\n\"Your content\" means your listings, photos, profile (name, photo, bio, company, city), messages, and reports.\n\n- You keep ownership of your content.\n- You give us a **non-exclusive, royalty-free, worldwide license** to host, store, copy, resize, display, and share your content to run, improve, and promote RenoSwap (for example, showing your listing on Browse or in a social media post about RenoSwap). This license ends when you delete the content or your account, except for copies we reasonably keep for backups, legal reasons, or safety records, and content already shared with other users (like messages you sent).\n- You promise you have the rights to what you upload (for example, you took the photos) and that it doesn't break the law or anyone's rights.\n- Don't post other people's personal information.\n\n## 8. Rules of conduct\n\nDon't:\n\n- Break the law or help anyone else break it.\n- List or trade anything on the [Prohibited Items list](/prohibited).\n- Post fake, misleading, duplicate, or bait-and-switch listings, or use RenoSwap to advertise off-site sales or services.\n- Scam, harass, threaten, discriminate against, or impersonate anyone.\n- Get around listing limits (for example, with multiple accounts) or misuse boosts, reports, or payments.\n- Scrape, copy, or collect data about users, or send spam.\n- Hack, overload, reverse-engineer, or interfere with the Service or its security.\n\n## 9. Suspension and ending your account\n\n- **You** can stop using RenoSwap anytime. To delete your account, use **Delete account** at the bottom of the **Account** page (or email RenoSwap101@gmail.com). Cancel any paid plan first (see Section 6). Deleting your account removes your listings, photos, alerts, and settings; people you messaged keep the conversation, shown as from a \"Deleted member.\"\n- **We** can suspend or close your account, remove content, or limit features at any time if we believe you broke these Terms, created risk or legal exposure, or to protect users. We'll try to tell you why, unless the law or safety reasons prevent it. If we close your account for breaking these Terms, you don't get a refund.\n- Sections that should survive after your account ends will (for example, Sections 7, 10–14).\n\n## 10. Disclaimers\n\nRenoSwap is provided **\"as is\" and \"as available.\"** To the fullest extent the law allows, we make **no warranties** of any kind, express or implied, including warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, title, and non-infringement. We don't promise that the Service will always be available, error-free, or secure, or that any user, listing, or item is safe, legal, accurate, or as described.\n\nRenovation materials can be heavy, sharp, or hazardous, and older materials may contain lead or asbestos. **You are responsible** for inspecting items, following safety rules and building codes, and handling, transporting, and disposing of materials properly.\n\n## 11. Limit on our liability\n\nTo the fullest extent the law allows:\n\n- We are **not liable** for anything that happens between users, including items, payments, meetups, pickups, injuries, property damage, or disputes.\n- We are not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or lost profits, data, or goodwill.\n- Our **total liability** for any claim related to RenoSwap is limited to the **greater of $100 or the amount you paid us in the 12 months before the claim**.\n\nSome laws don't allow some of these limits. If so, they apply only as far as the law allows.\n\n## 12. Disputes between users; your promise to cover us\n\n- **Disputes between users are between those users.** You release RenoSwap LLC and its owners, employees, and agents from claims arising from your dealings with other users, to the extent the law allows. We may, but don't have to, help.\n- **Indemnity.** You agree to defend and cover us (including reasonable attorney fees) against claims from others that come from your content, your listings or deals, your breaking these Terms, or your breaking the law.\n\n## 13. Disputes with RenoSwap\n\n- **Talk to us first.** Please email RenoSwap101@gmail.com with your concern. Most problems can be solved quickly. Give us 30 days to try to resolve it before filing a claim.\n- **Texas law.** These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of Texas, without regard to conflict-of-laws rules.\n- **Where cases go.** Any lawsuit must be brought in the state or federal courts located in **Lavaca County, Texas**. Either of us may instead bring an eligible claim in **small claims court (justice court)** in the Texas county where you live or in Lavaca County.\n- **No arbitration.** These Terms don't require arbitration.\n\n## 14. Other terms\n\n- **Changes.** We may update these Terms. If a change is significant, we'll let you know (for example, by email or a notice on the site) before it takes effect. If you keep using RenoSwap after that, you accept the new Terms. We may ask you to agree again.\n- **Whole agreement.** These Terms, the Privacy Policy, and the Prohibited Items list are the whole agreement between you and us about RenoSwap.\n- **If a part is invalid,** the rest still applies.\n- **Not giving up rights.** If we don't enforce something right away, we can still enforce it later.\n- **Transfer.** You can't transfer your account or these Terms. We may transfer them, for example if RenoSwap is sold.\n- **Events outside our control.** We're not responsible for delays or failures caused by things we can't reasonably control, like outages at our service providers, storms, or power failures.\n\n## 15. Contact\n\nRenoSwap LLC\n404 W McKinney St, Moulton, TX 77975-5008\nRenoSwap101@gmail.com\n";
export const privacy = "**Effective date:** October 15, 2026 · **Version:** 1.0\n\nThis policy explains what information RenoSwap collects, how we use it, who can see it, and your choices. RenoSwap is run by RenoSwap LLC (\"we,\" \"us\").\n\n**The short version:** we collect what we need to run a local materials marketplace. **We don't sell your personal information, and we don't show ads.** Your profile and listings are public. Your messages are private between you and the other person, but our admins can read them to keep people safe. Card details are handled by Stripe, not us.\n\n## 1. What we collect\n\n**Information you give us:**\n\n- **Account:** email address and password. Your password is handled by our login provider (Supabase Auth) and stored in a scrambled (hashed) form. We can't see it.\n- **Profile:** display name, role (Homeowner or Contractor), company name (if you're a contractor), city, ZIP code, a short bio, and a profile photo (optional).\n- **Listings:** title, category, condition, description, what you're looking for in a swap, price, city and ZIP, pickup/shipping options, the listing type (Swap, Sell, Sell or Swap, Fast & Free), and photos.\n- **Messages and offers** you send to other users.\n- **Reports** you file about listings or users, including your reason and details.\n- **Trades, ratings, and reviews:** trades you mark complete or confirm, star ratings and comments you leave, and reports about reviews.\n- **Alerts and email settings:** your \"Looking for\" alerts and whether offer, message, and alert emails are on or off.\n- **Support emails** you send us.\n\n**Billing information:**\n\n- If you buy a plan or a boost, **Stripe** collects your payment card and billing details. **We never receive or store your full card number.**\n- We keep your billing status: your plan, whether it's active, when it renews or ends, a Stripe customer ID, and which listings you boosted.\n\n**Information collected automatically:**\n\n- **Login cookies.** We use a small number of cookies to keep you signed in and secure your session. We **don't** use advertising or tracking cookies.\n- **Basic logs.** Our hosting and database providers automatically record technical information like IP address, browser type, pages requested, and the time, for security and to fix problems.\n\nWe don't currently send browser push notifications, and we don't collect your precise location. We only know the city and ZIP you type in. **Distance on Browse is approximate**: we estimate it from ZIP codes (for example, \"~12 mi\") and never show your address. **Photos:** when you upload a photo, the app strips GPS location data from the image file before it's stored.\n\n## 2. What's public and what's private\n\n**Public (anyone, even without an account, can see):**\n\n- Your **display name, profile photo, city, bio, company name, and Contractor label**\n- Your **approved listings**, including photos, description, price, and **city and ZIP**\n- Your **star rating and reviews** from completed trades (reviews appear once both people have left one, or after 7 days)\n\nOnly put in your profile and listings what you're comfortable sharing publicly. **Don't put your street address or phone number in a listing.** Share those in private messages only when you're ready.\n\n**Private:**\n\n- **Your email address** isn't shown on the site. *(See the note for the owner at the end of this document.)*\n- **Messages and offers** can only be seen by the people in the conversation and by **RenoSwap admins**. Admins may review them to check reports, stop scams or abuse, or enforce our Terms.\n- **Reports** can only be seen by the person who filed them and by admins.\n- **Billing details** are only visible to you, our admins, and Stripe.\n\n## 3. How we use your information\n\n- To create and run your account, and to show your profile and listings\n- To review and approve listings, and to handle reports\n- To let you message other users and make offers\n- To process subscriptions and boosts (through Stripe) and apply your plan's listing limits\n- To send account emails, like sign-up confirmations and password resets, and important notices about your account or policy changes\n- To send **email alerts** you can control: new offers and messages, and \"Looking for\" matches. Every alert email has an **unsubscribe** link, and you can turn alerts on or off on the Account page\n- To keep RenoSwap safe: preventing fraud, spam, and abuse, and enforcing our Terms\n- To fix bugs and improve the Service\n- To follow the law and respond to valid legal requests\n\nWe don't send marketing emails without your permission. We don't use your information for advertising.\n\n## 4. Who we share it with\n\n**We don't sell or rent your personal information.** We share it only:\n\n- **With other users**, as described in Section 2\n- **With service providers** that run RenoSwap for us, only as needed to provide their services:\n  - **Supabase:** database, login, and file storage (profiles, listings, photos, messages)\n  - **Vercel:** website hosting (and the basic logs described above)\n  - **Stripe:** payments and billing\n  - **Resend:** sends account emails and email alerts\n- **For legal reasons:** if the law requires it, to respond to valid legal requests, or to protect the rights, safety, or property of our users, the public, or RenoSwap\n- **If the business changes hands:** if RenoSwap is sold or merged, your information may transfer to the new owner, who must follow this policy or tell you about changes\n\nOur providers may store data on servers outside Texas, including elsewhere in the United States.\n\n## 5. How long we keep it\n\n- We keep account, profile, and listing information while your account is open.\n- Rejected or expired listings may stay in our records so admins can review history.\n- When you delete your account, we delete your profile, listings, photos, alerts, and settings right away. Messages you sent stay visible to the other person, shown as from a \"Deleted member,\" and remaining records are deleted or de-identified, usually within **30 days**. Some things may stay longer:\n  - copies in backups, until they expire\n  - billing and payment records we must keep for tax and accounting\n  - records of reports or rule violations kept for safety\n  - messages you sent may still be visible to the other person if they're kept for a report\n- Hosting and database logs are kept for a limited time by our providers.\n\n## 6. Your choices and rights\n\n- **Edit your profile** anytime on the Account page, including adding, changing, or removing your photo.\n- **Edit or remove listings** from My listings, or ask us to remove them.\n- **Cancel a plan** from Billing → Manage billing.\n- **Delete your account** yourself anytime: tap **Delete account** at the bottom of the Account page and type DELETE to confirm. Or email RenoSwap101@gmail.com from the email address on your account.\n- **Turn email alerts off** on the Account page, or use the unsubscribe link in any alert email.\n- **Get a copy or correct your information:** email us and we'll help.\n\nDepending on where you live, you may have additional privacy rights. Contact us and we'll respond as the law requires. We won't treat you differently for using your privacy rights.\n\n## 7. Security\n\nWe use reasonable safeguards: encrypted connections (HTTPS), hashed passwords, database access rules that limit who can see what, and trusted providers. No website is perfectly secure, so use a strong, unique password and tell us right away if you think your account was misused.\n\n## 8. Age limit\n\nRenoSwap is for adults **18 and older**. We don't knowingly collect information from children under 13. If you think a child has given us information, contact us and we'll delete it.\n\n## 9. Changes to this policy\n\nIf we make significant changes, we'll let you know (for example, by email or a notice on the site) before they take effect. The date at the top shows the latest version.\n\n## 10. Contact\n\nRenoSwap LLC\n404 W McKinney St, Moulton, TX 77975-5008\nRenoSwap101@gmail.com\n";
export const prohibited = "**Effective date:** October 15, 2026\n\nRenoSwap is for **leftover renovation and construction materials, fixtures, and tools**. Most leftovers are fine to list, like lumber, tile, drywall, doors, cabinets, fixtures, paint that's still sealed, and tools. But some things are dangerous, illegal, or need special disposal. **Don't list the items below.** Admins will reject or remove them, and repeat or serious violations can get your account closed.\n\nThis list isn't complete. If something is illegal to sell or give away in Texas or under federal law, it's not allowed even if it's not listed here. When in doubt, leave it out, or email RenoSwap101@gmail.com and ask.\n\n## Hazardous building materials\n\n- **Asbestos.** Anything that contains asbestos or is likely to, unless it's been tested and shown to be asbestos-free. Older materials are the main risk, especially from homes built before about 1980: some vinyl floor tiles and sheet flooring and their glue, popcorn ceiling material, pipe and duct insulation, some roofing and siding shingles, and **vermiculite** insulation.\n- **Lead paint.** Painted items from before 1978 (doors, trim, windows, cabinets, and so on) may have lead paint.\n  - **Don't** describe them as \"lead-free\" or \"safe\" unless they've been tested.\n  - If you list older painted items, **say so clearly** in the description (for example, \"Painted before 1978, may contain lead paint, not tested\").\n  - Don't list lead paint chips, dust, or scraped debris.\n- **Used chemically treated wood that needs special disposal**, such as used **railroad ties** or **utility poles** (creosote-treated), and old **CCA-treated** (\"green\") lumber torn out of decks or playsets. New, unused pressure-treated lumber is OK.\n- **Mold or water-damaged materials**: visibly moldy drywall, insulation, carpet, or wood.\n- **Materials from fire or flood cleanups** that may be contaminated.\n\n## Chemicals, fuels, and pressurized containers\n\n- **Open or partly used containers** of solvents, thinners, strippers, degreasers, adhesives with hazard warnings, concrete or masonry acids, pool chemicals, and other hazardous chemicals. **Sealed, unopened** common products like latex paint, caulk, or grout are OK.\n- **Pesticides, herbicides, and termite treatments**, opened or not.\n- **Refrigerants** (like R-22 or R-410A) in cans or cylinders.\n- **Fuel and gas:** gasoline, kerosene, diesel, and **propane or other gas cylinders**, even empty ones.\n- **Unlabeled containers**, or anything in a container that isn't its original one.\n- **Damaged, swollen, or leaking batteries**, including lithium tool batteries.\n- **Mercury-containing items** that are broken, such as old thermostats or fluorescent tubes.\n\n## Safety risks and recalls\n\n- **Recalled products**, such as tools, heaters, electrical panels or breakers, and ladders. Check before listing at **[CPSC.gov/Recalls](https://www.cpsc.gov/Recalls)**.\n- **Damaged or modified electrical items**, like cut or frayed cords, burned or melted outlets and breakers, or fixtures with exposed wiring. Working used electrical items are OK if you describe their condition honestly.\n- **Damaged safety equipment**, like cracked hard hats, used or damaged fall-protection harnesses, or broken ladders.\n- **Gas appliances with known leaks or damage.**\n\n## Stolen goods and ownership problems\n\n- **Stolen items**, or anything you don't have the right to sell or give away.\n- **Jobsite materials that aren't yours.** If a client or employer paid for the leftovers, get their permission first.\n- Items with serial numbers removed or altered.\n- **Salvaged materials taken without permission** from buildings, construction sites, or demolition sites.\n\n## Always-prohibited items\n\n- **Weapons**, ammunition, explosives, and fireworks\n- Illegal drugs and drug paraphernalia; alcohol; tobacco and vape products; prescription medicines\n- **Counterfeit** or knock-off branded goods\n- Live animals\n- Anything else that's illegal to sell, give away, or own\n\n## Not allowed as listings\n\n- **Services instead of materials**: labor, installation, hauling, demolition, contractor ads, or job postings. Tools and equipment are fine to list.\n- **Spam, fake, or misleading listings**, including stock photos, bait-and-switch prices, duplicate posts, or \"contact me off-site for a better deal.\"\n- **Ads for another business or website**, or listings that just collect contact information.\n- **Trash or junk dumping**: things no one could reasonably reuse. (It's fine to mark reusable items \"Dumpster-bound\" to get them rescued.)\n- Listings that include someone else's personal information, or offensive, hateful, or adult content.\n- Anything that breaks our [Terms of Service](/terms) or the law.\n\nBefore you meet up, read our [safety tips](/safety).\n";
export const safety = "**Effective date:** October 15, 2026\n\nRenoSwap doesn't handle payment or pickups, so a little caution goes a long way.\n\n**Before you meet**\n\n- Keep talking in RenoSwap messages until you're ready to meet, so there's a record if something goes wrong.\n- Ask for extra photos and measurements. Confirm the quantity, condition, and price before you drive over.\n- **Never pay in advance** to someone you haven't met. Avoid wire transfers, gift cards, crypto, and \"I'll overpay, send me the difference\" offers. Those are common scams.\n- Don't share your home address until you're ready to arrange pickup.\n\n**Meeting up**\n\n- If you can, meet in a **public, well-lit place** during the day, like a store parking lot or a police station \"safe exchange\" spot.\n- For large items that need a home pickup, **have someone with you**. Or do a porch or driveway pickup so no one has to come inside. Tell a friend where you're going.\n- Trust your gut. If something feels off, leave.\n\n**Paying and inspecting**\n\n- Look the item over before you pay. Check for damage, moisture, mold, and missing parts.\n- Use a payment method you trust, and **only pay once you have the item**. Cash is simple. With payment apps, be sure you know who you're paying.\n\n**Loading and handling**\n\n- Bring the right vehicle, straps, tarps, and a helper. Many materials are heavier than they look.\n- Wear gloves and closed-toe shoes. Watch for nails, sharp edges, and broken glass.\n- **Don't sand, cut, or scrape** old painted or older building materials without proper precautions. They may contain lead or asbestos.\n- In Texas heat, bring water and don't overdo heavy lifting.\n\n**If something goes wrong**\n\n- Use **Report** on the listing or user, and email RenoSwap101@gmail.com.\n- If you're in danger or a crime has happened, call **911** or your local police.\n\nRead the [Prohibited Items list](/prohibited) and [Terms of Service](/terms). RenoSwap is only a venue, isn't part of any deal, and isn't liable for meetups.\n";
